From cfbe287eb272668d315dad395dc4d8a3e3c226ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Feb 2026 08:17:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Qt: Add general section to slides.json for slide type
 configuration
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a top-level "general" object to slides.json that lets the slide deck
configure the visual appearance of each slide type without any C++ changes.
The initial use-case is gradient colours for the banner widget background.

JSON structure:

  "general": {
      "slide_types": {
          "events":      { "color_start": "#rrggbb", "color_end": "#rrggbb" },
          "sponsorship": { "color_start": "#rrggbb", "color_end": "#rrggbb" },
          "tips":        { "color_start": "#rrggbb", "color_end": "#rrggbb" }
      }
  }

C++ changes (info_banner_widget):
- Add SlideTypeConfig struct (color_start, color_end) to the header.
- Add slide_type_configs_ map (BannerSlideType → SlideTypeConfig).
- loadSlidesFromResource() now parses "general.slide_types" and populates
  the map before parsing the slides array; works for both default and
  custom JSON resources, with custom entries overriding defaults.
- gradientForType() is now a const method that consults slide_type_configs_
  and falls back to the built-in palette when a type is absent.

doc/README.slides documents the new section, including how custom JSON
files can override colours for retheming without touching the source tree.

https://claude.ai/code/session_01UEpD4kktUn2RSQ2d4guPrt
