+Welcome Page Banner Slides
+==========================
+
+The welcome page in Wireshark and Stratoshark displays a rotating banner
+carousel with slides for events, sponsorship, and tips.  Slide content is
+loaded from JSON resource files at startup rather than being hardcoded.
+
+This document explains how the system works and how distributors or
+developers can add custom slides.
+
+
+Source Files
+------------
+
+  resources/json/slides.json              Default slide deck (shipped in source tree)
+  resources/json/banners/                 Banner images referenced by slides
+  ui/qt/widgets/info_banner_widget.h      BannerSlide / SlideTypeConfig structs and widget
+  ui/qt/widgets/info_banner_widget.cpp    JSON loading and rendering logic
+  ui/qt/CMakeLists.txt                    QRC generation (Wireshark)
+  ui/stratoshark/CMakeLists.txt           QRC generation (Stratoshark)
+
+
+JSON Schema
+-----------
+
+Slide files use the following top-level structure:
+
+  {
+      "schema_version": 1,
+      "general": { ... },   // optional – configures slide-type appearance
+      "slides":  [ ... ]    // required – array of slide objects
+  }
+
+
+General Section
+---------------
+
+The optional "general" object configures global presentation settings that
+apply to all slides.  Currently it supports one sub-key: "slide_types".
+
+  "general": {
+      "slide_types": {
+          "events": {
+              "color_start": "#1a4a6e",
+              "color_end":   "#234d6e"
+          },
+          "sponsorship": {
+              "color_start": "#2d4a3e",
+              "color_end":   "#1e3a32"
+          },
+          "tips": {
+              "color_start": "#4a3d6e",
+              "color_end":   "#3a2d5e"
+          }
+      }
+  }
+
+slide_types keys:
+
+  events       Configuration for event/conference slides.
+  sponsorship  Configuration for sponsorship slides.
+  tips         Configuration for tips/tricks slides.
+
+Per-type fields:
+
+  color_start  CSS hex colour string (#rrggbb or #aarrggbb) for the start
+               of the 145-degree background gradient.
+  color_end    CSS hex colour string for the end of the gradient.
+
+Both colour fields are optional.  If a type is omitted from slide_types,
+or if the general section is absent entirely, the widget falls back to its
+built-in default colours for that type.
+
+Custom JSON files (see "Custom Slides for Distributors" below) can also
+provide a general section.  Its slide_types entries are merged with (and
+override) those from the default slides.json, allowing distributors to
+retheme the carousel without touching the default file.
+
+
+Slides Array
+------------
+
+Each entry in the "slides" array is an object:
+
+  {
+      "type":            "events",
+      "tag":             "Conference",
+      "title":           "SharkFest'26 US",
+      "description":     "Nashville, Tennessee",
+      "description_sub": "July 18-23, 2026",
+      "body_text":       "Join the annual Wireshark developer and user conference...",
+      "button_label":    "Learn More",
+      "url":             "https://sharkfest.wireshark.org/sfus/",
+      "image":           "sharkfestus.png",
+      "date_from":       "2025-12-01",
+      "date_until":      "2026-07-23"
+  }
+
+Field reference:
+
+  schema_version   Required (top-level). Must be 1 or higher.
+  slides           Required (top-level). Array of slide objects.
+
+Per-slide fields:
+
+  type             Required. One of: "events", "sponsorship", "tips".
+                   Maps to BannerSlideType enum. Unknown types are skipped
+                   with a warning.
+  tag              Optional. Short label shown as a pill/badge above the
+                   title (e.g. "Conference", "Tip of the Day").
+  title            Optional. Main heading text.
+  description      Optional. Primary text shown in the highlight box.
+  description_sub  Optional. Secondary line in the highlight box.
+  body_text        Optional. Additional paragraph below the highlight box.
+  button_label     Optional. Text for the action button.
+  url              Optional. Target URL opened when the slide or button
+                   is clicked.
+  image            Optional. Filename of a banner image resolved at runtime
+                   under :/json/banners/.  If empty or missing a
+                   semi-transparent overlay is shown instead.
+  date_from        Optional. ISO 8601 date (YYYY-MM-DD). The slide is
+                   hidden before this date.
+  date_until       Optional. ISO 8601 date (YYYY-MM-DD). The slide is
+                   hidden after this date.
+
+Slides without date fields are always visible (subject to the per-type
+visibility preference).  Slide strings are intentionally not translatable;
+content changes frequently and translation lag would be worse than
+untranslated text.
+
+
+Banner Images
+-------------
+
+Place image files in resources/json/banners/.  All files in this directory
+are automatically picked up by CMake (via file(GLOB)) and embedded in the
+Qt resource system under the :/json/banners/ prefix.
+
+No CMake changes are needed when adding or removing images.
+
+Recommended dimensions: 600×240 px (2× the logical 300×120 display area,
+suitable for HiDPI/Retina).  The image is scaled to fill the illustration
+area and center-cropped.  Top corners are rounded with an 8 px radius, so
+avoid placing critical content in the top ~10 px corners.
+
+
+Custom Slides for Distributors
+------------------------------
+
+Distributors can inject additional slides and override slide-type colours at
+build time without modifying the source tree.
+
+CMake cache variable:
+
+  CUSTOM_SLIDES_JSON    Path to a custom slides JSON file.
+
+Usage:
+
+  cmake -DCUSTOM_SLIDES_JSON=/path/to/my_slides.json ..
+
+The custom file must use the same JSON schema as slides.json.  It is
+embedded as :/json/slides_custom.json and loaded after the default slides.
+If the path does not exist it is silently ignored.
+
+Custom slides are appended after the default slides.  If the custom file
+also contains a "general" section its slide_types colour entries override
+the defaults from slides.json, allowing full retheming.
+
+Example custom_slides.json:
+
+  {
+      "schema_version": 1,
+      "general": {
+          "slide_types": {
+              "events": {
+                  "color_start": "#5a1a6e",
+                  "color_end":   "#3a0d4e"
+              }
+          }
+      },
+      "slides": [
+          {
+              "type":         "events",
+              "tag":          "Local Event",
+              "title":        "Wireshark Meetup",
+              "description":  "Your City, Your Country",
+              "description_sub": "March 15, 2026",
+              "body_text":    "Join us for a local Wireshark user group meeting.",
+              "button_label": "RSVP",
+              "url":          "https://example.com/meetup",
+              "image":        "",
+              "date_from":    "2026-02-01",
+              "date_until":   "2026-03-15"
+          }
+      ]
+  }
+
+
+Adding a New Default Slide
+--------------------------
+
+1. Edit resources/json/slides.json and add a new entry to the "slides" array.
+
+2. If the slide needs a banner image, place the file in
+   resources/json/banners/ and set the "image" field to the filename.
+
+3. Use date_from and date_until to time-limit the slide when it is for a
+   specific event.
+
+4. Rebuild.  CMake picks up new banner images automatically; no other file
+   changes are required.
+
+
+Changing Slide-Type Colours
+----------------------------
+
+Edit the "general.slide_types" section in resources/json/slides.json and
+set the hex colour values for the gradient start and end points.  The
+change takes effect after a rebuild; no C++ changes are needed.
+
+  "general": {
+      "slide_types": {
+          "events": {
+              "color_start": "#rrggbb",
+              "color_end":   "#rrggbb"
+          }
+      }
+  }
